title: "Recovered or Repaired? Harness, three-round oracle, and run records"
version: "1.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24271570
type: software
abstract: >-
  Code and data for the paper "Recovered or Repaired? A Three-Round External Oracle for LLM Agents on Backend Incident
  Remediation": the three-round external oracle, the experiment harness, the faulty releases of the order service, the
  port of the oracle to SREGym, the pre-registration log, every run record, and the scripts that regenerate the tables
  and figures of the paper. Code is under the MIT license; data and documentation are under CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA).
